          "text": "## Publication\n\nNational Institute of Child Health and Human Development, NIH, DHHS. April 2000. NIH publication 00-4754. The official catalog identifies this as the full subgroup report; a shorter summary and a topic findings webpage are separate presentations of the panel's work.\n\n## Scope and interpretation\n\nSynthesizes research on reading instruction across alphabetics, fluency, comprehension, teacher education and computer technology. Findings vary by instructional component, learner group and outcome.\n\nThis historical research synthesis is distinct from the later Reading First funding evaluation. Its included studies, summary report and full subgroup report are not independent program trials.\n\nThe panel's topic-specific reviews are background for reading instruction. The Reading First impact study evaluates implementation of a later funding program, not a direct replication or test of every panel finding. No pooled effect sizes from the panel report have been extracted into this dataset.\n\n## Sources\n\n[Full report and chapters](https://www.nichd.nih.gov/publications/pubs/nrp/report); [official publication catalog](https://www.nichd.nih.gov/publications/product/247); [topic findings](https://www.nichd.nih.gov/publications/pubs/nrp/findings).",
          "spaceId": "dac259bad48a11adf97fe36857d85206",
          "entity": {
            "id": "01cb53238c4e4be4a824bcd6dedf6683",
            "name": "National Reading Panel: publication and scope",
            "description": null,
            "types": [
              {
                "id": "76474f2f00894e77a0410b39fb17d0bf",
